    {
      "id": "4qzdggf",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Background: Rise of New Religions"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Jainism details the Founder, Tirthankaras, Teachings of Mahavira, and the Three Jewels of Jainism (Triratna).",
        "Key structural developments in Jainism include the Jain Councils, Jain Sects, and its historical contributions.",
        "Buddhism focuses on the Life of Gautama Buddha, the Four Noble Truths, and the Eightfold Path.",
        "Essential study areas for Buddhism include the Buddhist Councils, Buddhist Sects, and Important Buddhist Literature."
      ],
      "id": "3x97gxc"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jvytdha",
      "content": "• By the 6th century BCE many people were dissatisfied with the complex rituals of Vedic religion."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0r8bc4o",
      "content": "• The dominance of Brahmins and rigid caste system created social tensions."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9dhnoed",
      "content": "• Expensive sacrifices (Yajnas) were difficult for common people."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1abnrvw",
      "content": "• As a result, new religious movements like Jainism and Buddhism emerged."
    },
    {
      "id": "4eca48w",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. Jainism"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "o8ppezg",
      "content": "Jainism is one of the oldest religions in India. It emphasizes non‑violence, self‑discipline and spiritual purity."
    },
    {
